# Normalise line endings in the repo to LF, regardless of the contributor's OS.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` (the default there) writes
# CRLF into the working tree. Prettier's `endOfLine: "lf"` then reports EVERY file as
# unformatted — ~615 of them — so `npm run format:check` is useless locally and the real
# offenders are impossible to spot. Unformatted files reached `main` repeatedly that way,
# and because the `build` job runs `format:check` before the Angular build, each one turned
# every open PR red regardless of its own diff.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores and checks out text files with LF everywhere, so a local
# `format:check` now agrees with CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
